          "title": "Diazotization Kinetics & Sandmeyer Synthesis of 4-Bromobenzonitrile",
          "difficulty": "Mastery",
          "statement": "Devise an efficient multi-step synthesis of 4-bromobenzonitrile starting from benzene.\n(a) Detail all reagents, temperatures, and intermediate structures.\n(b) Explain why bromination cannot be performed directly on benzonitrile.\n(c) Detail the mechanism of the Sandmeyer substitution with copper(I) cyanide, identifying the oxidation state of copper and the radical intermediates involved.",
